WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.111
Ever followed a list of steps to make something?

00:00:03.161 --> 00:00:06.858
Native Hawaiian weavers have done it for generations.

00:00:07.208 --> 00:00:13.444
Lauhala is the dried leaf of the hala tree, woven into mats, baskets, even sails.

00:00:13.994 --> 00:00:19.871
To make a rose, a weaver goes step by step: leaf, strip, fold and roll, rose.

00:00:20.521 --> 00:00:23.087
A sequence of steps that finishes a task?

00:00:23.137 --> 00:00:24.596
That's an algorithm.

00:00:24.646 --> 00:00:28.204
And anyone can follow one, a person or a machine.

00:00:28.954 --> 00:00:32.630
Now let's look at an algorithm a computer can execute.

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:37.013
A program is an algorithm written so a computer can run it.

00:00:37.063 --> 00:00:40.324
Under When run, each block is one instruction.

00:00:40.674 --> 00:00:43.958
Press Run, and the tablet does every step on its own.

00:00:44.008 --> 00:00:46.485
Nobody has to choose what comes next.

00:00:47.535 --> 00:00:51.173
But what if we swap two steps? Now the path goes wrong.

00:00:52.323 --> 00:00:56.375
Is it still an algorithm? Yes. Just a wrong one.

00:00:57.125 --> 00:00:58.880
So, the steps come first.

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:02.815
A program is steps written so a computer can run them.
